# Copy to `.env.production` and fill in from the Supabase dashboard:
#   Project Settings -> API -> Project URL, and the `anon` `public` key.
#
# `.env.production` is COMMITTED on purpose. Both values below are compiled
# into the JS bundle every visitor downloads, so neither is a secret - the anon
# key is an identifier, and Row Level Security is the actual access control.
#
# The `service_role` key is the opposite: it bypasses RLS entirely. It must
# never appear in this file, in any other .env, in the bundle, or in CI. If a
# design seems to need one in the browser, the RLS policies are wrong.
#
# With these absent the app builds and runs exactly as the offline hot-seat
# game - see src/features/multiplayer/onlineConfig.utils.ts.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
